VERDICT
  scintillation: the true sigma2_I stays inside +/-15% of its unobscured value up to eR/w0 ~ 0.22; beyond that the obscuration lifts it while Dios stays flat.
  by eR/w0 ~ 0.44 the true sigma2_I is 1.5x its unobscured value; Dios, reading only w0, reports no change.
  mean power: the FULL fidelity-1 budget carries this loss in its tx_gaussian_efficiency_term (it reads the obscuration). It matches the wave-optics far-field within 0.4 dB across the whole sweep (up to 2 dB at eR/w0 ~ 0.44), slightly conservative. NOT a blind spot.
  So the one fidelity-1 blind spot is the SCINTILLATION: the coupled-flux kernel reads only w0, so its sigma2_I stays flat while the true index rises with the obscuration. Trust the fidelity-1 FADE only for a small obscuration relative to the beam (eR/w0 well below 1).

